{"id":"e552011c9a419872e1f4dde2b669da270311acfd","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"e552011c9a419872e1f4dde2b669da270311acfd","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/modules-dir-outside-the-project.md","lines":["@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@"," \"pacquet\": patch"," ---"," ","-Fixed installs in a workspace whose `modulesDir` is an absolute path or starts with `..`. A fresh install no longer puts the dependencies of workspace projects outside the workspace. A frozen install now links the root project's dependencies into the configured directory. pnpm now also removes a dependency you remove from such a directory. With `excludeLinksFromLockfile`, the root project's linked dependencies now go to the configured directory. The root project's lifecycle scripts now find the commands of its dependencies. The `loaded` node linker now puts the root project's commands in that directory's `.bin` [pnpm/tasks#285](https://github.com/pnpm/tasks/issues/285).","+Fixed installs in a workspace whose `modulesDir` is an absolute path or starts with `..`. A fresh install no longer puts the dependencies of workspace projects outside the workspace. A frozen install now links the root project's dependencies into the configured directory. pnpm now also removes a dependency you remove from such a directory. With `excludeLinksFromLockfile`, the root project's linked dependencies now go to the configured directory. The root project's lifecycle scripts now find the commands of its dependencies. The `loaded` node linker now puts the root project's commands in that directory's `.bin`. `pnpm bin` and `pnpm root` now print the directories the install uses. `pnpm run`, `pnpm exec`, and `pnpm version` now find a project's commands there [pnpm/tasks#285](https://github.com/pnpm/tasks/issues/285)."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/bin.rs","lines":["@@ -33,8 +33,7 @@ impl BinArgs {","                 .applies_package_configs()","                 .then(|| pnpm_